<title>SINGAPORE: Shareholder sells 19 percent Heshe stake.</title>
<headline>Shareholder sells 19 percent Heshe stake.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A substantial shareholder has entered into an agreement to sell a 19 percent stake in retailer Heshe Holdings Ltd, Heshe said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement Tan Sim Chew was disposing of 59.2 million shares at Singapore $0.45 per share, totalling S$26.6 million.</p>
<p>The completion date was fixed for September 23, 1997 or such other postponed date as the vendor may agree, the statement said.</p>
<p>The statement did not name a buyer.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
